k nearest neighbour classification problem

in which a point comes in between two classes and the problem arises where this point belongs 1 or 0.

so we use k value than can be any value for exmaple 1, 2 ,3 ,4 ,5. these values tells how many neighbour will be around that point. the side which has most closest
neighbour will included that point in that side.

so we need to find the closest neighbour around that unidentified class point in between.
so we need to use a distance formula.

1 is eullidean distance called crow distance where it reaches through shortest distance to its destination.
1 is manhattan distance called taxi path distance where a taxi follows the road path to the destination.
distance formula for 2d where x and y exist.
underroot (x2 - x1)^2 + (y2 -y1)^2.

so it depends on the problem statement which distance technique we would use. but mostly eullidean distance is used 
we basically check the most accuracy we get from and use that one. with also doing hyperparameter tunning

k nearest neighbour regression problem

it is much easier
when a points came between two classes unidentified we just select a k value and find the closest neighbour and take the avg of those group of neighbour
and if we hvae outliers we take the median of that group.


